# Deny by default. This repository sits on top of raw Twitter/X data that must not be
# published: tweet text, usernames, profile bios (which contain scraped email addresses)
# and user ids. Rather than list what to exclude and risk missing a file, everything of a
# data-bearing type is ignored and the release artifacts are allow-listed at the bottom.
#
# Before the first commit, check `git status --porcelain` and confirm that no parquet,
# pickle, coding file or built report appears.

# --- data-bearing formats, ignored wholesale -------------------------------------------
*.parquet
*.pkl
*.jsonl
*.ipynb
*.log

# --- the private corpus ----------------------------------------------------------------
# snapshot/ is the working data: actors.csv carries usernames, bios and the email
# addresses scraped with them, and corpus.parquet carries tweet text. Only the anonymized
# derivative under release/ is publishable.
snapshot/
actor_ideology_affiliation.csv

# --- built reports: these inline every actor's username and bio ------------------------
*.html
report_data.json
.report/

# --- fit cache and run outputs ---------------------------------------------------------
exp/fits/
exp/logs/
# `final2-pick` writes these to the working directory; paper/ holds the copies the
# write-up includes, so the root ones are regenerable output rather than source.
/fit_final2_concepts.csv
/fit_final2_edges.csv

# --- the superseded code and data kept locally for reference only ----------------------
old/

# --- environment and tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# --- LaTeX build products --------------------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls

# --- allow-list: the release data and the paper's artifacts ----------------------------
# The release data is a derivative: pseudonymous actor ids, no tweet text, no bios.
# Built by make_release_data.py, which documents what is dropped and why.
!release/
!release/snapshot/
!release/snapshot/*.parquet
!release/snapshot/*.jsonl

# The codebook is the paper's instrument and carries no personal data.
!ideology_nodes_v3.csv
!ideology_edges_v3.csv
!ideology_forbidden_edges_v3.csv

# The report template is source, not a built report.
!report_template.html
